WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:10.927
Subtitles are color-coded by country,
and this setting cannot be changed.

2
00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:13.722
Stand by.

3
00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:23.314
Ready…

4
00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.619
Yes! That's it!

5
00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.079
Throw her over!

6
00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:46.212
-Don't fall out of bounds!
-Don't fall out!

7
00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:49.507
I tried to throw her over by her leg,
but she didn't even budge.

8
00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:50.967
I guess she's a wrestler for a reason.

9
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.218
Grab her. That's okay.

10
00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.720
Grab both of her legs together!

11
00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:54.637
Hang in there!

12
00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.723
Her foot is off the edge.
Push her foot off!

13
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:02.645
Come on, you got this.

14
00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.067
Push her now!

15
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.193
Push her off!

16
00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:18.495
Stop.

17
00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:20.080
Game over.

18
00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.167
Here is the country surviving
after the second round.

19
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.210
Japan.

20
00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.298
Well done! Good job!

21
00:01:31.132 --> 00:01:31.966
Thank you!

22
00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:36.137
I should've held out a bit longer.

23
00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:38.515
If only I'd done a better job.

24
00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.433
I kind of beat myself up afterward.

25
00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.477
I did it!

26
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.937
NONOKA OZAKI
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

27
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.149
I was ecstatic
that we'd won such an intense match.

28
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:51.903
I felt a deep sense of pride inside.

29
00:01:57.408 --> 00:02:01.079
I was over the moon
about our win against Korea.

30
00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:04.833
Man, that was just the best.

31
00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:07.710
Now that we're down to
the one final stage,

32
00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.339
we absolutely have to make sure
that we win this quest

33
00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:15.135
and earn the right to set the matchups,
as it's an incredible advantage.

34
00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.095
It's disappointing

35
00:02:17.929 --> 00:02:19.681
and hard to get over,

36
00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:21.975
but it's actually strengthened my resolve.

37
00:02:22.058 --> 00:02:24.227
Next time we meet, you're dead meat.

38
00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:25.812
I'll crush you.

39
00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.230
Just you wait.

40
00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:31.109
Here are the results
of the second round's rematch.

41
00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:33.111
The countries advancing to the third round

42
00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:35.196
are Türkiye and Japan.

43
00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:38.992
Final match.

44
00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.246
What do you think their game plan is?

45
00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.916
Türkiye

46
00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.043
has huge players.

47
00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.546
YOSHIO ITOI
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM BASEBALL PLAYER

48
00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:54.841
And from their previous matches,

49
00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:58.803
I got the impression
that they always have a defined strategy.

50
00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:01.139
They had one player who didn't
take part in the game at all.

51
00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:02.223
KANA WATANABE
MMA FIGHTER

52
00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:04.392
There was always a female player

53
00:03:04.475 --> 00:03:08.479
standing on the sidelines, monitoring
the situation and calling out the time.

54
00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:09.939
How many minutes?

55
00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.357
One minute and thirty-five seconds.

56
00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:12.692
Thirty-eight seconds!

57
00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:15.028
Watch out, two of them are outside!

58
00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.571
Five seconds!

59
00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:17.488
Nefise!

60
00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.240
Get up! You have to come!

61
00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:24.537
NEFISE KARATAY
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM TRACK ATHLETE

62
00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:26.831
I noticed that

63
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:30.627
and shared it with my teammates.

64
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.128
SOICHI HASHIMOTO
NATIONAL TEAM JUDOKA

65
00:03:32.837 --> 00:03:35.006
Let's each mark one of their players…

66
00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:36.424
KANA WATANABE
MMA FIGHTER

67
00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:37.926
…and finish with a one-on-one
between her and Kana.

68
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:41.179
You know their female wrestler?

69
00:03:41.262 --> 00:03:42.347
I think she's strong.

70
00:03:43.431 --> 00:03:44.974
YASEMIN ADAR YIĞIT
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

71
00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.018
We should basically consider her a man.

72
00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.021
I guess I'm the one who has to take her.

73
00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:51.689
I was nervous

74
00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:53.524
because our weight classes were different.

75
00:03:53.608 --> 00:03:57.111
She's a world champion
in the highest weight division, the 76 kg,

76
00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:59.447
while I'm in the one below.

77
00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:04.160
I never imagined
I'd face her in a wrestling match.

78
00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.829
They're scared of us.

79
00:04:07.705 --> 00:04:08.623
Not to mention tired.

80
00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:10.208
-They're tired.
-They are.

81
00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:12.252
RECEP KARA
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM OIL WRESTLER

82
00:04:12.335 --> 00:04:14.087
Japan and Korea have had many rematches.

83
00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.131
Four or five of them, in fact.

84
00:04:17.215 --> 00:04:18.508
We'll win this easily.

85
00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.968
YASEMIN ADAR YIĞIT
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

86
00:04:20.843 --> 00:04:23.972
Let's finish this in one go
without going into a rematch.

87
00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:25.390
-Yes, let's do that.
-Yeah.

88
00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:28.226
Make sure we block at least one of them.

89
00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:31.813
The strategy is the same.
Protect us, Allah.

90
00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.734
Physical: Asia.

91
00:04:37.318 --> 00:04:40.571
Final round of the territory conquest.

92
00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.032
You will fight to conquer…

93
00:04:44.909 --> 00:04:46.452
a single territory.

94
00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:53.543
The game will now begin.

95
00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.256
We'll show them
how strong the Japanese are.

96
00:04:58.339 --> 00:05:00.008
We got this. Go Japan!

97
00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:07.557
We, Team Türkiye,
will go all out and claim the victory.

98
00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.767
Well said. Short and sweet!

99
00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:11.811
Come on!

100
00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:34.042
PHYSICAL: ASIA

101
00:05:36.586 --> 00:05:40.590
3. SHIPWRECK

102
00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:43.426
Stand by.

103
00:05:44.927 --> 00:05:45.970
Let's go!

104
00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.181
Ready…

105
00:06:02.278 --> 00:06:03.112
-Go, go!
-Go!

106
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.698
-Come on! Leg it, leg it!
-That's it!

107
00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.286
Take them out. Get them away!

108
00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.252
The big guy's going for Okami.

109
00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.427
Okami's gone flying.

110
00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:34.519
My sole target
was the leader of Team Japan.

111
00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:36.646
My focus was only on him.

112
00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:41.150
I was in the middle of
fighting other players

113
00:06:41.651 --> 00:06:44.153
when Recep seized me from behind.

114
00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:46.989
That was a painful mistake.

115
00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:54.664
No! Don't let him go!

116
00:06:56.707 --> 00:06:57.834
It was all going to plan.

117
00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:01.963
Each player guards their target,
releasing them at the last minute

118
00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:05.591
to run inside without them.

119
00:07:05.675 --> 00:07:08.761
I thought, "What are these people doing?
What's going on here?"

120
00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:11.639
I was getting nervous

121
00:07:11.722 --> 00:07:13.474
that we were going to lose.

122
00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:18.604
They've pinned down one contestant each.

123
00:07:20.481 --> 00:07:21.566
That's their strategy.

124
00:07:21.649 --> 00:07:22.859
The entire fight is
happening off the territory.

125
00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:33.953
I'm taking her down.

126
00:07:36.747 --> 00:07:38.499
Ali, you just get in here.

127
00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:40.501
She's wrestling
while holding that guy's leg.

128
00:07:42.378 --> 00:07:43.963
That Turkish girl is insanely strong.

129
00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:52.847
I need to dig deep for my team.

130
00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.432
Yes! Yes!

131
00:08:01.272 --> 00:08:02.106
Oh, she's…

132
00:08:03.274 --> 00:08:04.859
She's really strong.

133
00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:09.197
Japan is really strong in wrestling.

134
00:08:09.739 --> 00:08:10.698
Wow. Damn.

135
00:08:13.784 --> 00:08:15.244
I was confident that I could beat her,

136
00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:17.914
so I decided to finish it off
right then and there.

137
00:08:20.374 --> 00:08:23.669
Come on, give it everything.
Let's go, girls!

138
00:08:24.629 --> 00:08:25.463
Go!

139
00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:28.466
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

140
00:08:29.425 --> 00:08:30.760
Ten seconds.

141
00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:31.969
We need one person!

142
00:08:33.262 --> 00:08:35.348
-Somebody get in here quickly!
-Get in here!

143
00:08:35.431 --> 00:08:36.432
Anyone!

144
00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.267
Seven seconds!

145
00:08:44.607 --> 00:08:45.566
Nefise, come on!

146
00:08:47.318 --> 00:08:48.402
Nefise, come on!

147
00:08:52.782 --> 00:08:54.242
Stop! Stay where you are!

148
00:08:54.325 --> 00:08:55.451
Don't move!

149
00:09:16.597 --> 00:09:17.598
Game over.

150
00:09:21.102 --> 00:09:22.812
-Recep got on.
-We won!

151
00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:30.278
We're the winners.

152
00:09:30.861 --> 00:09:32.154
Everyone!

153
00:09:32.863 --> 00:09:34.448
-Look at this right here!
-Bravo!

154
00:09:36.534 --> 00:09:37.577
Bravo!

155
00:09:42.331 --> 00:09:43.583
That was amazing.

156
00:09:43.666 --> 00:09:44.667
Absolutely phenomenal.

157
00:09:52.508 --> 00:09:55.761
At the last second…

158
00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:57.555
SOICHI HASHIMOTO
NATIONAL TEAM JUDOKA

159
00:09:57.638 --> 00:10:01.684
…I got thrown by Anıl, and we lost.

160
00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:03.603
I messed up.

161
00:10:03.686 --> 00:10:05.146
I didn't manage to take Recep down.

162
00:10:07.189 --> 00:10:09.567
Türkiye…

163
00:10:10.067 --> 00:10:12.528
Türkiye ended up winning

164
00:10:13.362 --> 00:10:17.199
despite our best efforts.

165
00:10:18.242 --> 00:10:20.161
Yes, I was mad as hell.

166
00:10:20.244 --> 00:10:21.287
YOSHIO ITOI
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM BASEBALL PLAYER

167
00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.497
I haven't been that mad in a long time.

168
00:10:23.998 --> 00:10:28.336
It was especially frustrating
to fall at the last hurdle.

169
00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:31.172
The first quest.

170
00:10:31.756 --> 00:10:33.090
The territory conquest.

171
00:10:33.674 --> 00:10:35.426
The final winner is

172
00:10:36.218 --> 00:10:37.219
Türkiye.

173
00:10:40.848 --> 00:10:42.725
-Good job, Japan.
-Well done, Japan.

174
00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:47.688
-One, two, three, Türkiye!
-One, two, three, Türkiye!

175
00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:54.654
We've now shown them the power of Türkiye.

176
00:10:54.737 --> 00:10:56.739
NEFISE KARATAY
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM TRACK ATHLETE

177
00:10:56.822 --> 00:10:57.990
We'd do anything for our country.

178
00:10:58.074 --> 00:10:59.533
OGEDAY
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM ROWER

179
00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:01.202
I'm not scared of anyone.
I want to compete against everybody.

180
00:11:01.285 --> 00:11:02.953
Everyone's going to fear us now…

181
00:11:03.037 --> 00:11:04.705
YASEMIN ADAR YIĞIT
NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

182
00:11:04.789 --> 00:11:08.167
…because we've proven how strong we are.

183
00:11:12.755 --> 00:11:13.589
Leader.

184
00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:15.341
Thank you.

185
00:11:29.814 --> 00:11:31.232
Türkiye

186
00:11:31.315 --> 00:11:34.693
has won the privilege
to set all the matchups

187
00:11:35.319 --> 00:11:38.239
for the following quest.

188
00:11:42.326 --> 00:11:43.536
-Lucky them.
-All of them?

189
00:11:43.619 --> 00:11:44.453
Yes, all of them.

190
00:11:44.537 --> 00:11:46.622
-No way.
-That's huge.

191
00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:50.709
Prior to setting the matchups,

192
00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:55.506
the keyword for the second quest
will be revealed.

193
00:11:55.589 --> 00:11:56.799
Oh my god!

194
00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:00.719
Physical: Asia.

195
00:12:01.929 --> 00:12:04.432
The keyword for the second quest is…

196
00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:10.354
"shipwreck."

197
00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:13.691
…"shipwreck."

198
00:12:14.525 --> 00:12:16.235
OGEDAY
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM ROWER

199
00:12:16.318 --> 00:12:17.945
We got it. This is ours.

200
00:12:20.448 --> 00:12:21.907
We got it. We can relax now.

201
00:12:23.033 --> 00:12:25.077
We were thrilled
when we heard the keyword.

202
00:12:25.161 --> 00:12:27.246
We assumed it would involve
pulling something up.

203
00:12:27.329 --> 00:12:32.126
You know, something
that requires strength or stamina.

204
00:12:32.209 --> 00:12:34.128
We're also confident
in our explosive power

205
00:12:34.628 --> 00:12:36.547
as well as endurance.

206
00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.424
We get to decide the matchups,

207
00:12:38.507 --> 00:12:39.800
so they better be scared of us.

208
00:12:52.396 --> 00:12:53.564
Who should we pick?

209
00:12:54.148 --> 00:12:55.858
I think we should pick

210
00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:58.027
the second team from Japan.

211
00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.945
The second team to the right.

212
00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.616
They're staring at us.

213
00:13:04.867 --> 00:13:06.243
I'm sure they're targeting us.

214
00:13:06.327 --> 00:13:07.369
That's fine.

215
00:13:08.454 --> 00:13:09.455
That one looks okay too.

216
00:13:09.538 --> 00:13:11.790
So that's Thailand,
and that guy's an actor.

217
00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:16.795
They're picking their opponent.
It could be us.

218
00:13:16.879 --> 00:13:18.881
The Philippines doesn't look bad either.

219
00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:24.261
They're looking at us.

220
00:13:24.345 --> 00:13:26.180
They're thinking that they'll choose us.

221
00:13:26.263 --> 00:13:27.348
-Yeah.
-Yeah, maybe.

222
00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:29.934
We were concerned if

223
00:13:30.017 --> 00:13:32.019
Türkiye would choose us because they won.

224
00:13:32.102 --> 00:13:35.189
So we were a little bit nervous
because they're much bigger than us.

225
00:13:35.272 --> 00:13:36.941
We were fine with
any other team but Türkiye.

226
00:13:37.024 --> 00:13:38.442
JANG EUN-SIL
FORMER NATIONAL TEAM WRESTLER

227
00:13:38.526 --> 00:13:42.238
Lots of teams don't want to face them.

228
00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:43.906
JAMES RUSAMEEKAE
FORMER VOLLEYBALL PLAYER

229
00:13:43.989 --> 00:13:47.159
We also want to avoid them,
as they were strong in the first quest.

230
00:13:48.869 --> 00:13:49.870
Now,

231
00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:55.709
the matchups for the second quest
of Physical: Asia will be announced.

232
00:13:57.127 --> 00:13:59.922
Team Leader of Türkiye, Recep Kara,

233
00:14:00.005 --> 00:14:03.842
please reveal
the first teams in each group.

234
00:14:03.926 --> 00:14:07.805
I guess they'll pit
the strong teams against each other.

235
00:14:07.888 --> 00:14:09.723
I'm so curious to see.

236
00:14:10.224 --> 00:14:12.601
If it's us against Korea,
we'd win, wouldn't we?

237
00:14:12.685 --> 00:14:14.812
Well, we're used to them, at least.

238
00:14:14.895 --> 00:14:18.816
Since Türkiye will have realized
how strong we are,

239
00:14:18.899 --> 00:14:22.278
I expected them to pit us
against a strong team

240
00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:25.281
like Korea or Australia.

241
00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:28.200
I'd be fine with Japan.
Let's settle the score with them.

242
00:14:29.076 --> 00:14:30.828
The matchups will now be revealed.

243
00:14:37.793 --> 00:14:39.086
The Philippines.

244
00:14:45.426 --> 00:14:47.887
Australia is better than Korea.

245
00:14:49.013 --> 00:14:51.015
Well, they've split us up in any case.

246
00:14:54.435 --> 00:14:55.769
The opposing teams

247
00:14:55.853 --> 00:14:59.023
in each group will now be revealed.

248
00:14:59.607 --> 00:15:00.524
Group A.

249
00:15:00.608 --> 00:15:03.402
Please reveal Team Japan's opponent.

250
00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.113
Please be good to us.

251
00:15:06.989 --> 00:15:11.076
Of course we'd like a team
with smaller players.

252
00:15:18.959 --> 00:15:20.586
All right, come on.

253
00:15:21.503 --> 00:15:22.338
Australia.

254
00:15:27.843 --> 00:15:28.761
Yeah!

255
00:15:33.599 --> 00:15:35.559
Yeah, they want the strong teams
to destroy each other.

256
00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.312
How do you two like that?

257
00:15:39.563 --> 00:15:43.651
We wanted the two strong teams,
Australia and Japan,

258
00:15:43.734 --> 00:15:46.779
to face each other in the opening match.

259
00:15:46.862 --> 00:15:48.364
We're going to win this match!

260
00:15:49.198 --> 00:15:51.158
I think they underestimate us,

261
00:15:51.241 --> 00:15:54.912
so we're going to prove
that Japan is the strongest team here.

262
00:15:54.995 --> 00:15:56.372
